  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "evidences": [
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "24695223"
      },
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "9159481"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Oligomer of 24 subunits (PubMed:9159481). There are two types of subunits: L (light) chain and H (heavy) chain (PubMed:9159481). The major chain can be light or heavy, depending on the species and tissue type. In the human liver, the heavy chain is predominant (PubMed:9159481). The functional molecule forms a roughly spherical shell with a diameter of 12 nm and contains a central cavity into which the insoluble mineral iron core is deposited (PubMed:9159481). Interacts with NCOA4; NCOA4 promotes targeting of the iron-binding ferritin complex to autolysosomes following starvation or iron depletion (PubMed:24695223)"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "SUBUNIT"
